                    <h1 class="detail-title" data-role="title">Viet Nam opens defense attach&#xE9; office in Chile</h1>
                    <h2 class="detail-sapo" data-role="sapo">
                        VGP - The inauguration ceremony of Viet Nam’s defense attaché office in Chile was held in Santiago, on November 11 (local time). 
                    </h2>
                    <div class="detail-info">
                        <div class="detail-author-top">
                            <p class="detail-author-top-content">
                                <a href="javascript:;" rel="nofollow" title="Thuy Dung" class="detail-author-top-name">Thuy Dung</a>
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="detail-time">
                            <div data-role="publishdate">
                                November 12, 2024 11:06 AM GMT+7

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="detail-content afcbc-body clearfix" data-role="content">
                        <figure class="VCSortableInPreviewMode" type="Photo" style=""><div><img data-author="" src="https://bcp.cdnchinhphu.vn/thumb_w/640/344443456812359680/2024/11/12/chile-1731382293441867726477.jpg" id="img_780636704203292672" w="777" h="501" alt="Viet Nam opens defense attaché office in Chile- Ảnh 1." rel="lightbox" photoid="780636704203292672" data-original="https://bcp.cdnchinhphu.vn/344443456812359680/2024/11/12/chile-1731382293441867726477.jpg" type="photo" style="max-width:100%;" width="" height="" data-nosnippet=""></div><figcaption class="PhotoCMS_Caption"><p data-placeholder="Nhập chú thích ảnh">President Luong Cuong (4th from left) and Minister of National Defense Phan Van Giang (5th from left) at the inauguration ceremony of Viet Nam’s defense attaché office in Chile, Santiago, November 11 (local time), 2024 - Photo: VNA</p></figcaption></figure><!-- bonewsrelation --><div class="VCSortableInPreviewMode  alignRight" type="RelatedNewsBox" data-style="align-right" relatednewsboxtype="type-2"><div class="kbwscwl-relatedbox type-2 baochinhphuen"><ul class="kbwscwlr-list"><li class="kbwscwlrl" data-date="12/11/2024 10:25" data-id="111241112090618852" data-avatar="https://bcp.cdnchinhphu.vn/344443456812359680/2024/11/12/chile-17313770408331439594079-45-0-461-665-crop-1731377046587524880145.jpg" data-url="/viet-nam-chile-issue-joint-statement-111241112090618852.htm" data-title="Viet Nam, Chile issue Joint Statement"><h4 class="kbwscwlrl-title"><a target="_blank" href="/viet-nam-chile-issue-joint-statement-111241112090618852.htm" class="title link-callout">Viet Nam, Chile issue Joint Statement</a></h4></li><li class="kbwscwlrl" data-date="09/11/2024 08:58" data-id="11124110908415246" data-avatar="https://bcp.cdnchinhphu.vn/344443456812359680/2024/11/9/ctn-1731116398140893395834-36-0-522-777-crop-17311164007941687441925.jpg" data-url="/state-leader-leaves-for-official-visits-to-chile-peru-and-apec-economic-leaders-week-11124110908415246.htm" data-title="State leader leaves for official visits to Chile, Peru, and APEC Economic Leaders’ Week"><h4 class="kbwscwlrl-title"><a target="_blank" href="/state-leader-leaves-for-official-visits-to-chile-peru-and-apec-economic-leaders-week-11124110908415246.htm" class="title link-callout">State leader leaves for official visits to Chile, Peru, and APEC Economic Leaders’ Week</a></h4></li><li class="kbwscwlrl" data-date="08/11/2024 15:05" data-id="111241108150544456" data-avatar="https://bcp.cdnchinhphu.vn/344443456812359680/2024/11/8/tta6491-1-15b49e7e0-0041-40c9-b71a-5347b5449234-17310273217351810075576-1731052883959996287591-0-0-486-777-crop-17310528889611996206734.jpg" data-url="/deputy-fm-highlights-significance-of-president-luong-cuongs-tour-to-chile-peru-111241108150544456.htm" data-title="Deputy FM highlights significance of President Luong Cuong's tour to Chile, Peru"><h4 class="kbwscwlrl-title"><a target="_blank" href="/deputy-fm-highlights-significance-of-president-luong-cuongs-tour-to-chile-peru-111241108150544456.htm" class="title link-callout">Deputy FM highlights significance of President Luong Cuong's tour to Chile, Peru</a></h4></li></ul></div></div><!-- eonewsrelation --><p>The event saw the participation of President Luong Cuong who is on an official visit to the South American nation, Chilean Defense Minister Maya Fernandez Allende, representatives of Chile's ministries and agencies, diplomatic delegation, and defense attaché offices in Chile.</p><p>Addressing the event, Vietnamese Minister of National Defense Phan Van Giang affirmed that Viet Nam firmly adheres to the foreign policy of independence, self-reliance, peace, friendship, cooperation and development, and proactive and active international integration. </p><p>In recent years, the Viet Nam People's Army has always been proactive in enhancing international integration and defense diplomacy, both bilaterally and multilaterally, achieving practical results, noted the minister. </p><p>Defense diplomacy has become one of the key pillars of the Party's foreign policy and State diplomacy and an important channel for building strategic trust, and developing friendly relations between Viet Nam and other countries and international organizations, thereby contributing to enhancing the country's position and prestige.</p><p>The defense attaché office at the Vietnamese Embassy in Chile will carry out defense diplomacy activities to promote mutual understanding and defense cooperation, making contributions to the development of Viet Nam-Chile comprehensive partnership.</p><p>Minister Maya Fernandez stated that within the framework of the traditional relations between the two nations, the defense sector plays an important role, which was addressed by both countries during the talks between President Gabriel Boric and President Luong Cuong, and it has been further concretized via a memorandum of understanding on defense cooperation.</p><p>She praised the decision of the Vietnamese Ministry of National Defense to open a defense attaché office in Chile, considering it an important milestone in the bilateral relations. </p><p>This move will help both sides continue to bolster collaboration in specific activities such as search and rescue, disaster prevention, as well as exchanging experiences and training personnel, emphasized the Chilean Minister./. </p><!--Tue Nov 12 2024 11:06:46 GMT+0700 (Giờ Đông Dương) --  -- Tue Nov 12 2024 11:06:46 GMT+0700 (Giờ Đông Dương)--><br />
                    </div>
                    




                </div>
            </div>
            
